KZ2 patch 7011: KZ2_PROF_STACK=1, caller chains for host profiler samples outside the exe.

An earlier change found 86 % of Gfx.Particles.UpdateJob's resident samples at one PC outside the exe (0x6fffffeff0d4, in a
Wine DLL): its SPU thread blocked in a system call. Patch 1033's sampler keeps only RIP, so it cannot say which call
or who made it. With KZ3_PROF=FROM,TO and KZ2_PROF_STACK=1, a sample whose RIP is outside the exe also scans the
suspended thread's stack from RSP up to its stack base (only within the thread's own stack reservation, recorded
when the thread is attached) for return addresses (a value inside a loaded module that follows a call instruction),
keeps up to 8 frames per (RIP, job) chain, stops after the second frame in the exe, and prints at the end
"[prof-stack] job=N n=COUNT rip=WHERE f0=... f1=..." for chains seen KZ2_PROF_STACK_MIN (default 20) times or more:
exe+0xRVA (resolve with nm) or module+0xOFF(nearest export+0xOFF). No unwinder and no lock in the sampler (the
module list is read once at the first sample). Off by default (one env lookup at profiler start, only when KZ3_PROF
is set); no behaviour change. A heuristic: a stale return address left on the stack can show up as a frame.

